# M7.4 acceptance: branding in the About dialog and the Preferences dialog.
#
# Run from the worktree root with an isolated HOME, an unreachable session bus
# (nothing reaches the user's config or keyring) and the M7.1 fake sidecar
# (no Claude calls, no network):
#
#   H=$(mktemp -d)
#   O=<repo>/.verify/m7.4/<impl|review|tester>
#   READER_SIDECAR_CMD="$PWD/tests/acceptance/m7.1-fake-sidecar.sh" \
#     scripts/shot.sh -o "$O" -s tests/acceptance/m7.4.steps -- \
#     env HOME="$H" DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/nonexistent \
#     ./build/app/agentic-reader
#   ctest --test-dir build -R branding --output-on-failure   # must pass
#
# Pass: shot.sh exits 0, every shot matches its comment, and the branding
# ctest passes.
#
# The app version is the project() VERSION in the top-level CMakeLists.txt
# (0.1.0 when these steps were written). The About dialog must show that
# exact version.
#
# Assumptions the steps rely on (the spec is silent):
#   - The menu bar reads File, Edit, Help. "&Help" has mnemonic H and its
#     About item (wxID_ABOUT) has mnemonic A. "&Edit" has mnemonic E and its
#     Preferences item has mnemonic P (as in M7.1).
#   - The About dialog is opened last and never closed: under Xvfb with no
#     window manager the GTK About box does not take keyboard focus, so
#     Escape would not reach it. shot.sh ends the app afterwards.
wait 2

# The main window (no title bar under Xvfb without a window manager). No
# visible text anywhere (menu bar, toolbar, chat pane, setup banner, status
# bar) contains "Claude Code".
shot main-window

key alt+e
wait 1
key p
wait 2

# The Preferences dialog is open. Its developer check box reads exactly
# "Use my local Claude Code login (developer)", unchecked, with its one-line
# personal-use warning. This label is the only text on screen that contains
# "Claude Code" (it is kept for the user's review in M8.0). No other label,
# button, title or message in the dialog contains "Claude Code".
shot preferences-dev-label

key Escape
wait 1

# The Preferences dialog is closed and the main window is back.
shot preferences-closed

key alt+h
wait 1
key a
wait 2

# The About dialog is open over the main window and shows:
#   - the name "Agentic Reader",
#   - the text "Powered by Claude." (for example "Agentic Reader. Powered by
#     Claude." or the name followed by a "Powered by Claude." line),
#   - the app version, 0.1.0 (the project() VERSION),
#   - no "Claude Code" anywhere,
#   - no Claude or Claude Code logo, no ASCII art, and no look-alike visual
#     (for example a terminal-style banner or an orange starburst). No image,
#     the app's own icon, or GTK's generic missing-image placeholder above
#     the name is fine.
shot about
